# pstack is mandatory

This repository is developed with Cursor's pstack plugin
(https://github.com/cursor/plugins/tree/main/pstack, v0.15.10+).
A vendored copy of the skills lives in `ncli/skills/pstack/` so every NCLI harness sees the same rules.

On every non-trivial task:

1. Start with `/poteto-mode` and follow the matched playbook.
2. Name the data shape before writing logic (`principle-model-the-domain`).
3. If the change crosses a module boundary, run `/architect`.
4. If the change looks small but could leak, run `/blast-radius` and prove the safety fact with a test or script.
5. Prefer `/tdd` when there is a cheap local test path.
6. Subtract dead code before adding (`principle-subtract-before-you-add`).
7. Before commit: `/deslop` and `/no-comments`.
8. README, AGENTS.md, and commit messages follow `/technical-writing`.

If pstack is not installed, fetch the plugin from the repo above and follow
`skills/poteto-mode/SKILL.md` yourself. Do not improvise a lighter process.

Forks in NCLI stay isolated (own memory, harness, worktree). Do not introduce a
global singleton session. New views are one file in `views/` with a default
export. Do not hand-register them. The agent inside NCLI follows `skills/*/SKILL.md`.
